{"profile":{"name":"Paul Ainslie","ward":"Ward 24, Scarborough—Guildwood","bio":"Paul Ainslie was first elected to Toronto City Council in 2006 (appointed to a vacant Ward 41 seat in February 2006, then elected in Ward 43 that October), and has represented Scarborough-Guildwood as Ward 24 since 2018. He has over 25 years of experience across federal, provincial, and municipal government and previously owned and operated a small business. In May 2025 he was appointed Deputy Mayor for Scarborough.","committees":["Executive Committee","General Government Committee (Chair)","Scarborough Community Council (Chair)","Toronto Zoo Board of Management (Chair)","Toronto and Region Conservation Authority Board of Directors (Vice-Chair)","Federation of Ontario Public Libraries Board of Directors (Past Chair)","Toronto Transit Commission","Exhibition Place Board of Governors","Service Excellence Committee (Vice-Chair)","Toronto Public Library Board","FIFA World Cup 2026 Subcommittee","Night Economy Champion","Two-Spirit, Lesbian, Gay, Bisexual, Transgender and Queer Advisory Committee","Guild Renaissance Group"],"contact":{"email":"councillor_ainslie@toronto.ca","phone":"416-392-4008"},"promises":[{"text":"Deliver public transit improvements for Scarborough, including an LRT along Kingston Road and Morningside Avenue — City funding secured, with work toward a commitment from the Province and Federal governments for their share.","source":"http://www.voteainslie.ca/residents-first.html"},{"text":"Build a Jobs Skills Centre in Scarborough at the former site of Sir Robert L. Borden BTI (200 Poplar Road) to train residents for long-term, good-paying jobs in the community.","source":"http://www.voteainslie.ca/residents-first.html"},{"text":"On public safety: introduce a 'seize and destroy' motion demanding the Province amend the law so seized illegal weapons are destroyed rather than put back on the streets.","source":"http://www.voteainslie.ca/residents-first.html"}]},"lobbying":{"to